<title>USA: Bellwether sells $100 mln in junk bonds.</title>
<headline>Bellwether sells $100 mln in junk bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following high-yield bond offering from Bellwether Exploration Corp was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager JP Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Bellwether, based in Houston, is a oil and gas exploration and production company.</p>
<p>BORROWER BELLWETHER EXPLORATION CORP</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	COUPON 10 7/8 PCT MATURITY 4/1/07</p>
<p>TYPE SR NOTES     ISS PRICE 100     FIRST PAY DATE 10/1/07</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B3   YIELD 10 7/8 PCT  PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS  SPREAD 400 BPS    CALLABLE NON-CALLABE FOR</p>
<p>							    FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>((Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
</text>
